(1, 1, 'Target Company', 'Target Role', 'React JS Developer\nCapgemini\n3.655.2K Reviews\nCompany Logo\n2 - 6 years\nNot Disclosed\nBengaluru\nSend me jobs like this\nPosted: 1 day ago\nApplicants: 100+\nSave\nApply\nFollow Capgemini as you apply to stay updated\nCompany Logo\nReact JS Developer\nCapgemini\n3.655.2K Reviews\nSend me jobs like thisApply\nJob highlights\n4+ years experience in Front-End Development with expertise in ReactJS, Redux, TypeScript, and Jest\nDevelop responsive web applications, convert UI/UX designs into reusable code, integrate REST APIs, optimize performance, and participate in code reviews\nJob description\nAt Capgemini Engineering, the world leader in engineering services, we bring together a global team of engineers, scientists, and architects to help the worlds mostinnovative companies unleash their potential. From autonomous cars to life-saving robots, our digital and software technology experts think outside the box as theyprovide unique RD and engineering services across all industries. Join us for a career full of opportunities. Where you can make a difference. Where no two days arethe same.\n\n\nJob Description\n\nReactJS Developer\nLocation :- Mysuru\nExperience :- 4+ years\nChoosing Capgemini means choosing a place where youll be empowered to shape your career, supported by a collaborative global community, and inspired to reimagine whats possible. Join us in helping organizations build modern digital experiences through innovative and scalable web applications.\nYour Role\nAs a ReactJS Developer, you will be responsible for developing high-quality, responsive, and performance-driven web applications using ReactJS and modern front-end technologies. You will collaborate closely with UI/UX designers, backend developers, and product teams to deliver seamless user experiences and scalable front-end solutions.\nIn this role, you will:\nConvert UI/UX wireframes and mock-ups into high-quality, reusable, and maintainable code.\nDevelop responsive and user-friendly web interfaces using ReactJS, Redux, and TypeScript.\nBuild reusable components and implement efficient state management solutions.\nIntegrate front-end applications with REST APIs and backend services.\nOptimize applications and components for maximum speed and scalability across devices and browsers.\nParticipate in code reviews, troubleshooting, debugging, and performance tuning activities.\nWrite and maintain unit test cases using Jest and React Testing Library.\nEnsure adherence to coding standards, design patterns, and front-end best practices.\nYour Profile\n610 years of experience in Front-End Development with strong expertise in ReactJS.\nStrong hands-on experience with JavaScript (ES6+), ReactJS, and modern front-end architecture.\nGood knowledge of HTML5, CSS3, Responsive Web Design, and cross-browser compatibility.\nExperience with Redux and/or Context API for state management.\nStrong understanding of React component lifecycle, hooks, and functional programming concepts.\nExperience consuming REST APIs and working with JSON data structures.\nProficiency with Git and source code management practices.\nFamiliarity with build and bundling tools such as Webpack, Vite, or Babel.\nPreferred / Nice-to-Have Skills\nHands-on experience with TypeScript.\nExperience in unit testing using Jest and React Testing Library.\nExposure to CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices.\nExperience working with AmCharts controls and data visualization frameworks.\nKnowledge of web performance optimization techniques.\nFamiliarity with Docker and containerized deployments.\nUnderstanding of Agile/Scrum development methodologies.\nAbout Us\nAt Capgemini Engineering, the world leader in engineering services, we bring together a global team of engineers, scientists, and architects to help the worlds most innovative companies unleash their potential. From autonomous cars to life-saving robots, our digital and software technology experts think outside the box as they provide unique RD and engineering services across all industries. Join us for a career full of opportunities. Where you can make a difference. Where no two days are the same.\nAt Capgemini Engineering, the world leader in engineering services, we bring together a global team of engineers, scientists, and architects to help the worlds mostinnovative companies unleash their potential. From autonomous cars to life-saving robots, our digital and software technology experts think outside the box as theyprovide unique RD and engineering services across all industries. Join us for a career full of opportunities. Where you can make a difference. Where no two days arethe same.\nRole: Full Stack Developer\nIndustry Type: IT Services & Consulting\nDepartment: Engineering - Software & QA\nEmployment Type: Full Time, Permanent\nRole Category: Software Development\nEducation\nUG: Any Graduate\nPG: Any Postgraduate\nKey Skills\nSkills highlighted with ‘‘ are preferred keyskills\nAgile\nArchitectureBabelDesign PatternsApisContext ApiData StructuresDebuggingDevopsCoding StandardsCss3Ci/Cd PipelinesDevops PracticesDockerData VisualizationDevelopment MethodologiesBrowser Compatibility', 92, '{\"personalInfo\":{\"name\":\"SIVAKUMAR SELVARAJ\",\"email\":\"sivakumarselvaraj1008@gmail.com\",\"phone\":\"+91 9361343013\",\"location\":\"Thiruthangal, Virudhunagar - 626130\"},\"summary\":\"Performance-driven React.js Developer with expertise in building responsive, scalable front-end interfaces and modular component architectures using modern JavaScript (ES6+), HTML5, and CSS3. Skilled in converting UI/UX wireframes into maintainable code, integrating REST API services, and optimizing web application performance across browsers. Proven track record of delivering production-ready web solutions within Agile/Scrum environments.\",\"skills\":[\"React.js\",\"JavaScript (ES6+)\",\"HTML5\",\"CSS3\",\"Responsive Web Design\",\"REST API Development\",\"Fetch API\",\"JSON\",\"UI/UX Development\",\"Wireframing\",\"Web Performance Optimization\",\"Core Web Vitals\",\"DOM Manipulation\",\"Async/Await\",\"Git\",\"GitHub\",\"Agile/Scrum\",\"Playwright Automation\",\"Load/Performance Testing\",\"Node.js\",\"Express.js\",\"MySQL\",\"CRUD\",\"Authentication\",\"Authorization\",\"npm\",\"VS Code\",\"Technical SEO\",\"Product Analytics\",\"Payment Gateway Integration\",\"Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)\",\"Pinecone\",\"Vector Databases\",\"XHAMPP\"],\"experience\":[{\"title\":\"Junior Full-Stack Engineer\",\"company\":\"Noxlay Cyber Tech\",\"dates\":\"May 2026 – Present\",\"bullets\":[\"Engineered core front-end architecture for multi-tenant SaaS platforms using modular, reusable React.js components and modern JavaScript (ES6+), earning 3 designations in 12 months for exceptional contributions.\",\"Converted UI/UX wireframes into responsive, cross-browser compatible web interfaces and integrated backend REST APIs including PhonePe payment gateways.\",\"Optimized application load speeds, database schemas, and Core Web Vitals to boost maintainability and overall user experience.\",\"Developed automated UI testing suites using Playwright, leveraging Agile/Scrum methodologies to deliver high-quality, production-ready web applications.\"]}]}', '2026-08-01 12:22:20'),
